  {
    "title": "Backoff, jitter and a budget",
    "body": "The fix has four parts. Retry at **one layer** only, here the phone, and let the others fail fast. Make **at most 3 attempts**. Wait longer each time, about 100 ms and then 200 ms (**backoff**), plus a random amount (**jitter**), so a thousand phones that failed together do not all retry at the same moment. And keep a **retry budget**: if retries pass 10% of requests, stop retrying, so a failing service sees at most about 1.1 times its normal load. Retry only requests that are safe to repeat (SD 7).",
